# Status (2026-10-05): open; a design question (the values of one Hash have one type).
# `**opts` collects keywords, but cannot pass them on: `f(**opts)` is "`**` is not supported".
# Passing the Hash itself (and reading it with Hash.fetch) loses each option's type: the values
# become one union, so `--strict` rejects String.split(s, sep) ("can be true|false").
# csv wants read(path, **opts) = parse(File.read(path), **opts), as Ruby's CSV.read.
def parse(s, sep: ",", headers: nil) = headers ? [headers, String.split(s, sep)] : String.split(s, sep)
def read(s, **opts) = parse(s, **opts)   # error: `**` is not supported
p read("a;b", sep: ";")
